  "answer": "The goal was met: five settings on five different scenes are confirmed hard, and each failed on every repeat (S7, S22, S12, S19, S28). But they are not the large-error, high-speed corners the brief asked about. The search never went past a 0.1 m sideways shift. In two of the five scenes (S7, S22), VaVAM fails with no shift at all and at recorded speed. In the other three, a +0.1 m shift to the left was enough: S12 and S19 at recorded speed, S28 at 1.2x. At that same speed, the unshifted runs in those scenes did not fail (S10, S17, S26), though they had few repeats. Every failure was the policy's fault and had the same pattern: the ego drifted left against a STRAIGHT or RIGHT route command, then either hit a car passing in the left lane or ran onto the left shoulder or median. The failures in S12 and S19 are flagged as possible simulator artifacts because the ego ended far from the recording. The triage puts this down to the drift itself, with a clear camera view. Each setting has only a few repeats, so the ranges confirm a failure rate above one half, not its exact value.",
